    points: ['New toilet and basin', 'Taps, waste and pipework', 'Tiling or wall panels', 'Old suite taken away'] },
  { id: 'full', tier: 'Full bathroom', popular: true, name: 'Full bathroom, supplied and fitted', price: '£4,995', from: true, unit: 'supplied and fitted, inc VAT',
    points: ['Bath or shower, toilet, basin and taps', 'Strip-out and disposal', 'All plumbing and tiling', 'Usually 5 to 7 working days'] },
  { id: 'pk-en-suite', tier: 'En-suite', name: 'En-suite shower room', price: '£4,495', from: true, unit: 'supplied and fitted, inc VAT',
    points: ['Shower tray, enclosure and valve', 'Toilet and basin', 'Tiling and waterproofing', 'Extractor fan by our partner electricians'] },
  { id: 'bath-to-shower', tier: 'Most asked for', name: 'Bath to shower conversion', price: '£2,395', from: true, unit: 'supplied and fitted, inc VAT',
    points: ['Bath removed and taken away', 'Tray, enclosure and thermostatic valve', 'Shower area tiled or panelled', 'Usually 2 to 3 days'] },
];

const faqs = [
  { q: 'How much does a bathroom installation cost on the Wirral?', a: 'A full bathroom on the Wirral, supplied and fitted, starts from £4,995 including VAT. An en-suite is from £4,495 and a cloakroom or WC is from £2,495. A bath to shower conversion is from £2,395. If you buy your own suite, a labour-only full refit is from £2,750. You get a fixed written price after a free home visit.' },
  { q: 'How long does a bathroom installation take on the Wirral?', a: 'A full bathroom usually takes 5 to 7 working days. A bath to shower conversion takes 2 to 3 days. A bathroom in a Victorian outrigger can take a little longer if the old waste pipes need replacing. We give you the dates in your quote.' },
  { q: 'Do you cover every Wirral CH postcode?', a: 'Yes. We fit bathrooms across CH41 to CH49 and CH60 to CH64. That takes in Birkenhead, Wallasey, Moreton, Hoylake, West Kirby, Heswall, Bebington, Bromborough and Neston. Travel is included in your quote.' },
  { q: 'Can you fit a new bathroom in a Victorian outrigger?', a: 'Yes. Many terraces in Birkenhead, Wallasey, Hoylake and Rock Ferry have the bathroom in the rear outrigger. These rooms often have long waste runs, old cast iron pipes and joists that need checking. We look at all of this at the free visit and price it before we start.' },
  { q: 'Will a new en-suite affect my water pressure?', a: 'It can. Two showers running at once can be weak on an old tank system. In larger homes in Heswall, Pensby and Bromborough, an unvented cylinder often fixes this. Our engineers are G3 qualified, so we can fit the cylinder and the en-suite as one job. Unvented cylinders start from £1,450.' },
  { q: 'Do I need a separate tiler or electrician?', a: 'No. Our team does the plumbing and the tiling. Lights, extractor fans and shower circuits are done by our partner firm Ideal Electrical Solutions. We book them into the same plan, so you only deal with us.' },
  { q: 'What if you find a problem under the old bath?', a: 'We show you and give you a price before we fix it. Old Wirral homes often hide a rotten board, a weeping waste or a corroded cast iron pipe. Nothing gets covered up, and you decide.' },
  { q: 'Do I need to pay up front?', a: 'Nothing is paid before the visit, and the visit is free. Payment terms are agreed in writing with your quote, before the job is booked in. We do not offer finance.' },
];
