  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="cost">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>How much does a bathroom installation cost on the Wirral?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">A full new bathroom on the Wirral starts from £4,995, supplied and fitted, including VAT. A bath to shower conversion starts from £2,395.</p>
      <div class="brx-table-wrap">
        <table class="brx-table stk stk-price">
          <thead><tr><th>Job</th><th>Price, inc VAT</th><th>Typical time</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td data-label="Job"><strong>Cloakroom or WC</strong></td><td data-label="Price, inc VAT">from £2,495</td><td data-label="Typical time">A few days</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Job"><strong>Bath to shower conversion</strong></td><td data-label="Price, inc VAT">from £2,395</td><td data-label="Typical time">2 to 3 days</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Job"><strong>En-suite shower room</strong></td><td data-label="Price, inc VAT">from £4,495</td><td data-label="Typical time">Set out in your quote</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Job"><strong>Full bathroom, supplied and fitted</strong></td><td data-label="Price, inc VAT">from £4,995</td><td data-label="Typical time">5 to 7 working days</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Job"><strong>Labour-only full refit (your own suite)</strong></td><td data-label="Price, inc VAT">from £2,750</td><td data-label="Typical time">5 to 7 working days</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <h3>What changes the price on the Wirral?</h3>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li><strong>Old pipes.</strong> Outrigger bathrooms often have corroded cast iron waste pipes. These are best replaced, not reused.</li>
        <li><strong>Moving things.</strong> Moving a toilet or waste costs more than keeping it in place.</li>
        <li><strong>The suite and tiles you pick.</strong> A freestanding bath or premium tiles cost more.</li>
        <li><strong>Room size.</strong> More wall and floor means more tiling.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We spot these at the free visit, so they are in your price from the start. Only need a new shower? See our <a href="/showers-liverpool">shower installation</a> prices, from £375 fitted.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="included">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>What is included in a Wirral bathroom installation?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Everything from the strip-out to the final clean. Your quote lists what is in and what is not.</p>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li><strong>Strip-out and disposal.</strong> The old suite and tiles leave with us. No skip on your drive.</li>
        <li><strong>All plumbing.</strong> New supply and waste pipes, run and clipped properly.</li>
        <li><strong>Tiling.</strong> James's team does the tiling, with the wet areas waterproofed first. Or we fit wall panels if you prefer.</li>
        <li><strong>The suite.</strong> Bath or shower, toilet, basin, taps and valves, fitted and sealed.</li>
        <li><strong>Electrics.</strong> Lights, extractor fans and shower circuits by our partner firm <a href="https://www.idealelectricalsolutions.co.uk">Ideal Electrical Solutions</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Making good.</strong> We test every joint, seal everything and clean before we leave.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>You can buy your own tiles or suite. If you supply the suite, the labour-only price is from £2,750.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="homes">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Can you fit bathrooms in Wirral outriggers and period homes?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Yes. Outrigger terraces and period houses are some of the most common homes we work in on the Wirral.</p>
      <h3>Outrigger bathrooms in Birkenhead, Wallasey and Rock Ferry</h3>
      <p>Many Victorian terraces in Birkenhead, Wallasey, Hoylake and Rock Ferry have the bathroom at the back. It is often the old outside toilet and washroom, or a single storey add-on.</p>
      <p>These rooms bring three common problems:</p>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li><strong>Long waste runs.</strong> The pipe to the soil stack is long, so it needs the right fall.</li>
        <li><strong>Old cast iron pipes.</strong> They are often corroded and need replacing.</li>
        <li><strong>Joists.</strong> Swapping a shower for a full bath means checking the floor can take the weight.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We check all three at the free visit. They go into your fixed price, not a surprise bill after the strip-out.</p>
      <h3>Period houses in West Kirby, Hoylake and Heswall</h3>
      <p>Older houses here often have solid outside walls and little space under the floor. We rarely chase pipes into solid walls. Instead we run them under timber floors or in neat boxing. We show you the pipe routes before we start.</p>
      <p>Want a period look? Freestanding baths, column basins and traditional taps all suit these homes. We can supply them at a range of prices.</p>
      <p>Solid walls also mean more condensation. A good extractor fan matters. Our partner electricians fit it as part of the same job.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="how">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>How long does a bathroom installation take on the Wirral?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">A full bathroom usually takes 5 to 7 working days. A bath to shower conversion takes 2 to 3 days.</p>
      <ol class="sg-steps">
        <li><strong>Free home visit (about 45 minutes).</strong> We measure up and check the pipes, waste and walls. In an outrigger, we check the joists and cast iron too.</li>
        <li><strong>Fixed written price.</strong> The full spec, written down. What is included is listed, and so is what is not.</li>
        <li><strong>Day 1: strip-out.</strong> The old bathroom comes out and leaves with us.</li>
        <li><strong>Days 1 to 3: first fix.</strong> New pipes and waste go in. Our partner electricians do any wiring. If we find rot or a leak, we show you and price it first.</li>
        <li><strong>Days 3 to 5: walls and floor.</strong> Boarding, waterproofing and tiling, or wall panels.</li>
        <li><strong>Final days: fit and hand over.</strong> The suite goes in. We test every joint, seal it all and clean the room.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Bigger rooms, a lot of tiling or a new layout take longer. Your quote gives you the dates.</p>
      <div class="brx-cta">
        <p><strong>Want a price for your Wirral bathroom?</strong> Book a free home visit. No pressure to book.</p>
        <a href={TEL} class="brx-btn">Call {PHONE}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="en-suite">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Can you add an en-suite in south Wirral?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Yes. En-suites start from £4,495. In bigger homes we often fit an unvented cylinder at the same time, so every shower has strong pressure.</p>
      <p>Lots of detached and semi-detached homes in Heswall, Pensby and Bromborough are adding an en-suite to the main bedroom. Most people want a strong mains pressure shower.</p>
      <p>The catch is hot water. An old tank in the loft may not feed two showers at once. An unvented cylinder gives mains pressure hot water to every bathroom. Our engineers are G3 qualified to fit and test them.</p>
      <p>We can do the en-suite and the cylinder as one project, with one price. See our <a href="/hot-water-cylinders-wirral">hot water cylinders on the Wirral</a>, from £1,450.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="which">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Which option is right for me?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Start with what is wrong with the room now. If only the bath is the problem, a conversion may be all you need.</p>
      <div class="sg-cols">
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Bath to shower, from £2,395</h3>
          <p>Best if you rarely use the bath, or getting in and out is hard. A low level tray makes the step much smaller.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Full bathroom, from £4,995</h3>
          <p>Best if the suite, tiles and pipes are all tired. Common in outriggers with old cast iron waste.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>En-suite, from £4,495</h3>
          <p>A shower room off a bedroom. Popular in larger south Wirral homes.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Cloakroom or WC, from £2,495</h3>
          <p>A toilet and basin downstairs or under the stairs. Small room, small budget.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:1rem;"><strong>Not sure?</strong> We will tell you honestly at the free visit, even if the cheaper option is the right one.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="postcodes">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Do you cover all Wirral CH postcodes?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Yes. We fit bathrooms right across the peninsula, from Birkenhead to West Kirby and down to Neston.</p>
      <div class="brx-table-wrap">
        <table class="brx-table stk">
          <thead><tr><th>Area</th><th>Postcodes</th><th>Typical homes</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td data-label="Area"><strong>Birkenhead and east Wirral</strong></td><td data-label="Postcodes">Birkenhead CH41, Rock Ferry CH42, Prenton CH43, Wallasey CH44, New Brighton CH45</td><td data-label="Typical homes">Victorian and Edwardian terraces, often with outrigger bathrooms</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Area"><strong>West and north Wirral</strong></td><td data-label="Postcodes">Moreton CH46, Hoylake CH47, West Kirby CH48</td><td data-label="Typical homes">Period houses with solid walls and high ceilings</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Area"><strong>South Wirral</strong></td><td data-label="Postcodes">Heswall CH60, Pensby CH61, Bromborough CH62, Bebington CH63, Neston CH64</td><td data-label="Typical homes">Larger detached and semi-detached homes adding en-suites</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>Travel is included in your quote, wherever you are on the Wirral.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="why">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Why choose us as your Wirral bathroom fitters?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">One team for plumbing and tiling, a fixed price in writing, and a 12-month guarantee on our work.</p>
      <div class="sg-cols">
        <figure class="sg-photo">
          <picture>
            <source type="image/webp" srcset="/images/jobs/bathroom-bath-shower-fitted-480.webp 480w, /images/jobs/bathroom-bath-shower-fitted-960.webp 960w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 400px" />
            <img src="/images/jobs/bathroom-bath-shower-fitted-960.jpg" alt="New bath and shower fitted by our bathroom team" width="960" height="1280" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </picture>
          <figcaption>A real job: new bath and shower fitted.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="sg-photo">
          <picture>
            <source type="image/webp" srcset="/images/jobs/shower-room-fitted-480.webp 480w, /images/jobs/shower-room-fitted-960.webp 960w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 400px" />
            <img src="/images/jobs/shower-room-fitted-960.jpg" alt="Shower room fitted by our team" width="960" height="1280" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </picture>
          <figcaption>A real job: shower room fitted.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li><strong>One team.</strong> Plumbing and tiling by James's team. No waiting a week for a tiler to turn up.</li>
        <li><strong>Fixed price in writing.</strong> If we find something behind the old bath, we price it before we touch it.</li>
        <li><strong>We know Wirral homes.</strong> Outriggers, cast iron waste and solid walls are checked at the visit.</li>
        <li><strong>Guaranteed.</strong> 12 months on our work, and £2 million public liability insurance.</li>
        <li><strong>Tidy.</strong> We clean up and take all the rubbish away with us.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</ServiceGuide>
